---
import Page from "../layouts/page.astro";
import { lastUpdated, operator } from "../operator";
---

<Page title="Privacy Policy" description="What Lardon collects, why, and the choices you have.">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    Lardon is a family cookbook app run by {operator.name}. This policy explains what we collect when
    you use Lardon, why, and what you can do about it. We don't sell your data, show ads or track
    you across other apps and websites.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details:</strong> your email address and name. If you sign in with Apple or
      Google, we also receive an identifier for that account and, if you allow it, your name and
      profile picture. If you use Apple's "Hide My Email", we only receive the relay address Apple
      gives us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sign-in data:</strong> one-time sign-in codes (stored hashed and valid for 5 minutes)
      and active sessions, including the IP address and device type they were created from.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you add to Lardon:</strong> recipes, photos, family groups and the people you
      share them with.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical logs:</strong> short-lived server logs of requests (such as the address
      requested and whether it succeeded), used to keep the service running and secure.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To create your account and sign you in.</li>
    <li>To store your recipes and share them with the family members you choose.</li>
    <li>To send you sign-in codes by email.</li>
    <li>To keep Lardon secure, prevent abuse and fix problems.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We process this data to provide the service you asked for and, for security logs, because we
    have a legitimate interest in keeping Lardon safe.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We only share data with the services needed to run Lardon:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts our servers, database, photo storage and email sending.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apple</strong> and <strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The people in your family groups can see the recipes and photos you share with them.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your account and content for as long as you have an account. Sign-in codes expire after
    5 minutes, sessions expire on their own, and server logs are deleted after a few days. When you
    delete your account, we delete your account details and the content only you have access to.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, or to delete your account and data. You
    can also object to how we use it or ask us to limit it. Email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${operator.contactEmail}`}>{operator.contactEmail}</a> and we'll reply within
    30 days. If you're unhappy with our answer, you can complain to your local data protection
    authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Lardon isn't intended for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top. For important changes, we'll let you
    know in the app before they apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {operator.name}, {operator.country}. Questions about privacy:{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${operator.contactEmail}`}>{operator.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
